# Git LFS for prebuilt APKs that git cannot carry.
#
# GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB on push, and Cromite's
# SystemWebView is 297 MB, so it cannot live in this repository's object
# database at all. Through LFS the history carries a ~130-byte pointer, which
# also means a later decision to move the WebView into its own project (the way
# AOSP keeps external/chromium-webview's prebuilt in a separate LFS repository)
# costs a delete rather than a history rewrite.
#
# Only the WebView is listed. LeanType.apk (12.5 MB), Via.apk (4.1 MB) and
# MiXplorer.apk (5.3 MB) are ordinary blobs; keeping them out of LFS keeps them
# out of the LFS bandwidth quota that every clone spends.
#
# git-lfs must be installed before "repo sync", or the checkout leaves the
# pointer file in place of the APK and the build fails on an APK that is not a
# zip.
prebuilt/CromiteWebView/*.apk filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
